    "model": "<p><b>(a)(i)</b> A data flow diagram is a <b>graphical representation</b> of the <b>flow of data</b> through an information system: where data comes from, how it is processed, where it is stored and where it goes.</p><p><b>(a)(ii)</b> A <b>context level DFD</b> shows the entire system as a <b>single process</b> with little or no detail about its internal operations, whereas a <b>Level 1 DFD</b> breaks that process down into its individual <b>sub-processes</b> and shows the data stores and how data flows between them.</p><p><b>(a)(iii)</b></p><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gane and Sarson DFD symbols: an arrow for a data flow, a rounded rectangle with an ID band for a process, a shaded square for an external entity, and an open-ended rectangle with an ID box for a data store.\"><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"55\"/><path d=\"M62 49 L72 55 L62 61\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"25\" width=\"70\" height=\"60\" rx=\"10\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"42\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"42\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"25\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.06)\"/><path d=\"M190 25 l-5 5 v60 h60 l5 -5\"/><path d=\"M345 40 H275 V70 H345\"/><line x1=\"295\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"295\" y2=\"70\"/></g><g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"40\" y=\"100\">Data flow</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"36\">1.0</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"65\">Verb phrase</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"100\">Process</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"60\">Entity</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"100\">External entity</text><text x=\"285\" y=\"59\">D1</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"59\">Name</text><text x=\"310\" y=\"100\">Data store</text></g></svg><figcaption>Gane and Sarson symbols: data flow, process, external entity, data store.</figcaption></figure><p>Data flow: an <b>arrow</b> labelled with the data. Process: a <b>rounded rectangle</b> with an ID band at the top. External entity: a <b>square</b> with a shaded (double) edge. Data store: an <b>open-ended rectangle</b> with an ID box (D1) on the left.</p><p><b>(b)</b></p><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 230\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Context diagram: Payroll Clerk sends hours worked to process 0 Payroll System; the process sends payslips to Employee and payroll updates to the Payroll Database data store.\"><defs><marker id=\"pa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></marker></defs><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"75\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.06)\"/><rect x=\"275\" y=\"60\" width=\"75\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.06)\"/><rect x=\"135\" y=\"45\" width=\"90\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" stroke=\"#F5C542\"/><line x1=\"135\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"225\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#F5C542\"/><path d=\"M220 180 H140 V210 H220\"/><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"210\"/></g><g stroke=\"currentColor\" marker-end=\"url(#pa)\"><line x1=\"85\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"133\" y2=\"80\"/><line x1=\"225\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"273\" y2=\"80\"/><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"178\"/></g><g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"47\" y=\"84\">Payroll Clerk</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"84\">Employee</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"57\">0</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"85\">Payroll</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"98\">System</text><text x=\"109\" y=\"72\">Hours worked</text><text x=\"249\" y=\"72\">Payslip</text><text x=\"225\" y=\"150\">Updated payroll details</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"199\">D1</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"199\">Payroll DB</text></g></svg><figcaption>Context diagram for the payroll system (data store shown, as credited in the CXC mark scheme).</figcaption></figure><p>[Diagram described] External entity <b>Payroll Clerk</b> → data flow <i>hours worked</i> → process <b>0 Payroll System</b>. Process 0 → data flow <i>payslip</i> → external entity <b>Employee</b>. Process 0 → data flow <i>updated payroll details</i> → data store <b>D1 Payroll Database</b>. (The calculation of net pay happens inside process 0.)</p>",
    "teacherTip": "<p>Mark scheme for (b): entities 2, process 1, data store 1, data flows 2, accuracy (including flow direction) 2. Note that the official example includes the payroll database on the context diagram; in general a context diagram shows only one process and the external entities, with stores appearing at Level 1, so follow the question. Common errors: mixing notations (Yourdon circles with Gane and Sarson squares); unlabelled arrows; flows labelled with verbs (\"calculate\") instead of data nouns; connecting the clerk directly to the database; adding several processes to a context diagram.</p>",
