  "intro": "<p><b>CAPE Information Technology Unit 1 · Paper 02 · Mock 2 (original practice paper)</b></p><ol><li>This paper consists of THREE sections and SIX questions: Section I (Module 1), Section II (Module 2) and Section III (Module 3).</li><li>Answer ALL questions. Each question is worth 15 marks.</li><li>Time: 2 hours 30 minutes. Plan about 25 minutes per question.</li><li>Label every part (a), (b), (i), (ii) and use the command word: <i>state</i> and <i>identify</i> need a short answer; <i>describe</i>, <i>explain</i>, <i>distinguish</i> and <i>justify</i> need developed points.</li><li>Where a question asks for a diagram (network, DFD, flowchart or sketch), draw it on paper and describe it in your answer box: name each symbol or device, its label and what it connects to.</li></ol><p class=\"tip\">Mock 2 examines information sources and selection criteria, data quality and manual versus automated processing, software types, users and HCI evaluation, the structure of the Web and HTML, categorising information, Level 1 DFDs and DFD errors, and algorithm characteristics, tracing and development.</p>",
