    "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> <b>HTML</b> (HyperText Markup Language) uses a fixed set of predefined tags to structure and display content such as headings, images and links in a web browser. <b>XML</b> (eXtensible Markup Language) uses tags that the author defines to describe, store and transport data (for example &lt;dish&gt;&lt;price&gt;), and does not specify how the data is displayed.</p><p><b>(b)</b> <b>Protocol:</b> https. <b>Domain name:</b> calypsocafe.bb (www is a prefix). <b>File:</b> menu.html. HTTPS (HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure) is the set of rules for transferring web pages between the web server and the browser, with the data encrypted so that it cannot be read in transit.</p><p><b>(c)</b> Computers locate each other by numeric IP addresses, not names. When the customer enters the URL, the browser sends the domain name www.calypsocafe.bb to a <b>DNS server</b>. The DNS server looks up the name (asking other DNS servers if necessary) and <b>returns the matching IP address</b>. The browser then connects to the web server at that IP address and sends an HTTPS request for menu.html, which the server returns for the browser to display.</p><p><b>(d)</b></p><pre>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Calypso Café Menu&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;!-- Menu page: update dishes below each week --&gt;\n  &lt;h1 style=\"color: darkblue;\"&gt;Calypso Café Menu&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;All our dishes are made with &lt;b&gt;fresh&lt;/b&gt; local ingredients.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Johnnycakes and saltfish&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Conch and dumplings&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Passion fruit cheesecake&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;img src=\"johnnycake.jpg\" alt=\"Golden johnnycakes on a plate\" width=\"300\"&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"booking.html\"&gt;Book a table&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</pre>",
    "teacherTip": "<p>Common errors: saying XML \"replaces\" HTML; giving \"calypsocafe\" without the top-level domain; describing DNS as \"the server that hosts the website\"; placing &lt;title&gt; in the body; using &lt;ol&gt; when an unordered list is asked for; &lt;img&gt; without alt; writing &lt;a&gt;booking.html&lt;/a&gt; without href; inline style written as style=color:darkblue (missing quotes) or as a separate CSS block (the syllabus asks for inline styling with the style attribute); improper nesting such as &lt;b&gt;&lt;p&gt;…&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;.</p>",
