    "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\"><b>Palm Beach Scooter Rentals</b> is replacing its paper rental book. In the new system a customer submits a rental request; the system checks the Scooters data store for an available scooter, records the rental in the Rentals data store and issues a rental agreement to the customer. When a scooter is returned, the system calculates the charge from the Rentals data store, sends an invoice to the customer and marks the scooter as available. A mechanic sends service reports that update the Scooters data store.</p><p class=\"passage\">A student's draft Level 1 DFD for this system contains the following: [Diagram described: (1) a data flow arrow from the external entity Customer goes directly into the data store D2 Rentals; (2) a process labelled \"3 Monthly Report\" receives data from D2 Rentals but has no output flows; (3) a process labelled \"4 Invoices\" sends an invoice to Customer but has no input flows.]</p>",
    "prompt": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Categorise EACH of the following pieces of information as <b>essential</b>, <b>desirable</b>, <b>extraneous</b> or <b>cosmetic</b> for designing the rental system, giving a reason: (i) the daily rental rate for each scooter; (ii) the number of tourists who visited Aruba last year; (iii) a friend's assurance that tourists always return scooters undamaged, given instead of any damage records; (iv) customers' preferred scooter colour. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Identify <b>TWO</b> of the errors in the student's DFD and explain how EACH should be corrected. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Draw a <b>Level 1 DFD</b> (Gane and Sarson) for the rental system with <b>THREE</b> processes. Describe your diagram in words. <i>(7 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[15 marks]</b></p>",
