    "prompt": "<p>With reference to an information technology problem that you have researched, answer the following questions.</p><p><b>(a)</b> Discuss the MAIN reason why you researched this problem. <i>[2 marks]</i></p><p><b>(b)</b> Discuss TWO causes of the problem identified in (a). <i>[4 marks]</i></p><p><b>(c)</b> Write a problem statement that may form the basis of a solution to the problem you have researched. <i>[3 marks]</i></p><p><b>(d)</b> A more detailed analysis of the problem may require the collection of data through direct observation. Outline FOUR guidelines that should be followed when conducting the observation. <i>[8 marks]</i></p><p><b>(e)</b> After the observation, you are still unclear about the way a small group of users work with the existing system. Identify ONE other data gathering technique, clearly explaining how the technique will enhance the research process. <i>[3 marks]</i></p><p><b>[20 marks]</b></p>",
