     "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> At the Seaside Pharmacy in Gros Islet, the staff cannot keep track of stock, so medicines such as insulin run out while other items expire on the shelves.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> One cause is that stock is recorded by hand on paper stock cards that are updated only at closing time. This leads to the cards showing more stock than is really on the shelf, so the pharmacist reorders too late and items run out.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> The pharmacists and counter staff at Seaside Pharmacy cannot tell how much of each medicine is in stock or when it will expire, because stock is recorded by hand on cards updated once a day. If this is not corrected, the pharmacy will continue to lose sales and write off expired medicine.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> When observing, I should get permission from the owner and inform the staff before I start, because this is ethical and the staff will not feel they are being spied on.</p>\n<p><b>(e)</b> I would use an interview with the small group of counter staff, so I can ask them to explain how they update the stock cards.</p>",
