     "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> Solution 1 is a prepaid student meal card with a commercial canteen point-of-sale package. It would let the cashier scan a card and deduct the cost, so no cash changes hands. Solution 2 is a custom online pre-ordering web app. It would allow students to order and pay before 10 a.m.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> Solution 1 is technically feasible because it runs on a standard PC with a barcode scanner. It is economically feasible because the school buys a tested package instead of paying a developer. It is operationally feasible because cashiers only need a short training session to scan cards.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> One disadvantage of Solution 2 is that it takes months for a developer to build and test.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> It is good to identify several solutions before choosing because the school can compare them to find the best one, and it has a back-up if the first choice fails.</p>",
