  "intro": "<p><b>1 hour 30 minutes · 60 marks.</b> This paper consists of THREE questions. Answer ALL questions. Each question is worth 20 marks.</p><p>All three questions are based on an information technology problem that <b>you have researched</b>. Choose ONE problem before you start and use it consistently: Question 1 asks you to define and analyse the problem, Question 2 to propose and evaluate solutions, and Question 3 to select and justify the optimal solution and choose suitable software. Answers that switch problems between questions lose marks.</p><p>The model answers in this paper all follow one problem: bookings at Blue Reef Divers dive shop in Kralendijk, Bonaire.</p><p class=\"tip\">This is a past CXC CAPE Information Technology Unit 1 Paper 032 paper (May/June 2014), used here as practice for Paper 03 (Module 3, problem-solving) and transcribed for class practice. The questions are copyright of the Caribbean Examinations Council (CXC). Mark guidance and model answers were prepared for this course by Kester Small.</p>",
