     "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> At the Windwardside Community Clinic on Saba, the reception staff book appointments in a paper book, so patients are double-booked and wait up to two hours.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> One cause is that appointments are recorded by hand in a single paper book that only the receptionist can see. This leads to copying errors when nurses' phone bookings are added later, so two patients are given the same slot.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> Another step is analysing the problem by gathering data. In this step tools such as interviews and observation are used to collect facts about how the current system works.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> (i) Interview, because there are only five managers, so I can talk to each one and ask follow-up questions to clarify what they mean. (ii) Questionnaire. (iii) Observation.</p>\n<p><b>(e)</b> One limitation of a questionnaire is that some people may not return it, and I cannot ask a follow-up question if an answer is unclear.</p>",
