    "genre": "Paper 032 structured responses: possible solutions and feasibility (20 marks)",
    "prompt": "<p>You have proposed several solutions to the problem you described in Question 1 (a), from which you will select an optimal solution.</p><p><b>(a)</b> Discuss THREE possible solutions for the problem you described in Question 1 (a). <i>[9 marks]</i></p><p><b>(b)</b> Evaluate the feasibility of EACH solution proposed in 2 (a). <i>[9 marks]</i></p><p><b>(c)</b> Explain the benefit of identifying several possible solutions prior to selecting your final solution. <i>[2 marks]</i></p><p><b>[20 marks]</b></p>",
    "min": 400,
    "max": 1000,
    "frame": "<p><b>(a)</b> Solution 1: ... This would work by ... It solves the problem because ...<br>Solution 2: ... It works by ... It addresses the cause ... by ...<br>Solution 3: ... It works by ... It helps because ...<br><b>(b)</b> Solution 1. Technical feasibility: ... Economic feasibility: ... Operational feasibility: ... Overall, ...<br>Solution 2. Technical: ... Economic: ... Operational: ...<br>Solution 3. Technical: ... Economic: ... Operational: ...<br><b>(c)</b> Identifying several solutions allows the analyst to compare ... It also ...</p>",
