     "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> Solution 1 is a commercial clinic management package on a local server. It would store all appointments in one database, so every staff member sees the same diary. Solution 2 is a cloud-based appointment scheduling service. It would book appointments online and send SMS reminders to patients.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> Solution 1 is technically feasible because it runs on a small server in the clinic and still works when the Internet link is down. It is economically feasible because it is a one-off licence cost with no developer needed. It is operationally feasible because receptionists and nurses can be trained in a few days.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> One disadvantage of Solution 2 is that it depends on the Internet connection.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> It is good to identify several solutions before choosing because the clinic can compare them to find the best one, and has a back-up if the first choice fails.</p>",
