     "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> At Old Road Fishermen's Co-operative in St. Kitts, the clerk records catches by hand in notebooks, so fishers are paid the wrong amounts and records are lost.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> One cause is that catch data is written by hand at a busy, wet landing site. This leads to figures being written unclearly and pages being damaged, so wrong weights are used to calculate payments.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> Another step is implementing the chosen solution. This involves installing the hardware and software, training users and changing over from the old system.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> (i) Interview, because there are only five managers, so I can talk to each one and ask follow-up questions to clarify what they mean. (ii) Questionnaire. (iii) Observation.</p>\n<p><b>(e)</b> One limitation of a questionnaire is that some people may not return it, and I cannot ask a follow-up question if an answer is unclear.</p>",
