    "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> The most feasible solution is Solution 1: mobile data capture with online forms and a cloud spreadsheet.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> <b>Strategy 1: Recording catches on a rugged tablet at the landing site.</b> This is justified because it removes handwriting at the wet, busy landing site, the first cause of the problem. A waterproof case protects the device, and drop-down lists mean the clerk taps instead of writing, which is faster and more accurate.</p>\n<p><b>Strategy 2: Using online forms that feed a cloud spreadsheet.</b> Each entry is stored once and appears immediately in the spreadsheet, so the double copying into the ledger is eliminated. Formulas calculate each fisher's weekly payment, so fishers can be paid on time, and the board can see up-to-date totals and charts.</p>\n<p><b>Strategy 3: Low cost using free software and existing skills.</b> The only purchase is a tablet and a mobile data plan, so the solution is economically feasible for a small co-operative. The clerk and treasurer already use spreadsheets, so training is short and user acceptance is likely.</p>\n<p><b>Strategy 4: Security and back-up.</b> The account is protected by a strong password with two-step verification, and only the clerk and treasurer can edit the spreadsheet; board members get view-only access. Data is stored online, so it is not lost if the tablet is damaged, and a monthly copy is downloaded to the office PC as a back-up. More boats and members can be added without extra cost.</p>\n<p><b>(c)(i)</b> I would select Solution 2, the commercial co-operative accounting and inventory package.</p>\n<p><b>(c)(ii)</b> This alternative is better than the custom scale app because it is available now at a known price, needs no specialist developer and runs on the office PC the co-operative already owns. It solves the second cause, double copying and slow month-end payments, by calculating payments and reports automatically, and the vendor provides training and support.</p>\n<p><b>(c)(iii)</b> One disadvantage is that catches must still be written on paper at the landing site and keyed in later, so handwriting errors are not removed, unlike the tablet solution. To compensate, the co-operative could introduce printed, pre-numbered landing slips with boxes for each species, have each fisher sign the slip to confirm the weight, and have the clerk key in slips the same day while they are fresh.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> The most appropriate type of software is presentation software, such as Google Slides or Microsoft PowerPoint, because it allows me to summarise each stage of the problem-solving process on slides with charts, photos of the landing site and a diagram of the new process, making the presentation clear and engaging for the class.</p>",
