     "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> At the Hopewell Community Library in Orange Walk, Belize, the librarians record loans on paper cards, so overdue books are not followed up and about 300 books have been lost.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> One cause is that loans are recorded by hand on index cards filed by title. This leads to overdue books never being found, because no one has time to check every card.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> Another step is reviewing and monitoring the solution. This involves checking whether the new system meets its objectives and making changes if needed.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> (i) Interview, because there are only five managers, so I can talk to each one and ask follow-up questions to clarify what they mean. (ii) Questionnaire. (iii) Observation.</p>\n<p><b>(e)</b> One limitation of a questionnaire is that some people may not return it, and I cannot ask a follow-up question if an answer is unclear.</p>",
