  "intro": "<p><b>1 hour 30 minutes · 60 marks.</b> This paper consists of THREE questions. Answer ALL questions. Each question is worth 20 marks.</p><p>This practice paper is built around the case of Hummingbird Ridge High School in the central stimulus. Read it first, then answer every question about that case, using the same facts throughout: Question 1 asks you to describe and analyse the problem and choose fact-finding techniques; Question 2 asks you to discuss and evaluate three given solutions; Question 3 asks you to select, justify and present a solution.</p><p>The model answers use the Hummingbird Ridge High School case given in the paper.</p><p class=\"tip\">Practice Examination 1 is an original practice paper written in the format of the past CXC CAPE Information Technology Unit 1 Paper 032, used here as practice for Paper 03 (Module 3, problem-solving) and transcribed for class practice. The Paper 032 format and question style are copyright of the Caribbean Examinations Council (CXC). Mark guidance and model answers were prepared for this course by Kester Small.</p>",
  "stimulus": "<p><b>School Management Information System</b></p><p>Hummingbird Ridge High School currently maintains student attendance, grades, discipline records and teacher reports manually. Teachers record information in paper registers while office staff use separate spreadsheets to prepare reports.</p><p>The school has identified several problems:</p><ul><li>Student records are duplicated.</li><li>Attendance reports are often inaccurate.</li><li>Parents receive report cards late.</li><li>Records are sometimes misplaced.</li><li>Preparing reports requires excessive staff time.</li></ul><p>The principal has decided that a computerised School Management Information System should be developed.</p>",
