     "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> A custom system is one developed specially for the school by a programmer. A commercial system is a ready-made package the school would purchase. A cloud-based system is one the school would subscribe to and use online through the Internet.</p>\n<p><b>(b)</b> The commercial system is technically feasible because it runs on a server on the school network. It is economically feasible because there are no development costs, only a one-off licence. It is operationally feasible because teachers can be trained in the summer holiday.</p>\n<p><b>(c)</b> One disadvantage of the custom system is that it is the most expensive and takes months to develop and test.</p>\n<p><b>(d)</b> A school should evaluate several solutions before choosing because it can compare them to find the best one, and has a back-up if the first choice fails.</p>",
